WEBVTT

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:19.850
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:19.850
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:19.850
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:49.270
Imperial Year 486, while visiting
a resort satellite called Kreuznach III...

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:53.100
...Siegfried Kircheis got involved in an
unexpected event during his brief vacation.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:56.260
Have a nice stay.

00:01:56.260 --> 00:01:56.750
Thank you.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:18.140
It seems you
saved my life.

00:02:18.140 --> 00:02:20.640
I must thank you, young man.

00:02:23.030 --> 00:02:25.770
I am Baron Keyserling.

00:02:25.770 --> 00:02:30.210
Thank you for rescuing me, even
though we haven't met before.

00:02:30.870 --> 00:02:31.990
Keyserling ?

00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:34.630
This is retired
Rear Admiral Keyserling ?

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:39.550
You must be Commander Kircheis.

00:02:39.550 --> 00:02:41.650
I apologize for the trouble.

00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:46.690
I'm the Chief Superintendent
of this town, Hoffmann.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:54.310
I very much appreciate that
you assisted us in this case.

00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.660
No, I was just
there by chance.

00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:01.600
Then I will have to
thank chance for this.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.900
By the way, about that man, it's been reported
that he was under the influence of drugs.

00:03:06.730 --> 00:03:13.320
In the last 50 years the use of a drug called Thyoxin has become prevalent in the Fleet and in rural areas.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:18.300
The man was liberated from the prison of reason by this drug and attacked that old man...

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.670
...I mean, Baron Keyserling.

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.410
Why are you telling
me about this ?

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:28.900
Such a thing must be kept
secret in an investigation.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:32.410
To tell you the truth...

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:38.200
...when military personnel are involved in crimes,
there are times we can't operate as we like.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:40.160
Military personnel ?

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:46.310
According to his ID the perpetrator is presently a chief petty officer, and yet an addict like that.

00:03:46.310 --> 00:03:52.650
Naturally, we suspect that the field that produces
drug addicts must be within his domain.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:56.400
If I understand you correctly, you believe
that the illegal distribution of the drug...

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.400
...is done by an organization
within the military ?

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.440
Yes, and
an organization.

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:05.490
It couldn't be
done by an individual.

00:04:05.490 --> 00:04:10.700
Those who produce the drug, those who sell it,
those who distribute the profits, and so on.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.200
Their operation is very profitable.

00:04:14.200 --> 00:04:16.300
They're working for a common goal
and are committed to one another.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.650
They won't rat
each other out.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.110
What is he
trying to tell me ?

00:04:22.110 --> 00:04:24.240
He's strangely theatrical.

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:30.850
Especially, if they use a route within the fleet,
it's very difficult for us to make an arrest.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:37.510
We hesitate to ask the cooperation of the Military Police unless there's a dire emergency of some sort.

00:04:38.800 --> 00:04:40.460
This is what military people say:

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.010
"Leave matters involving military personnel to the Military Police."

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.200
I see.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.320
You'd like me to cooperate with you on
your investigation of this drug organization.

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:55.490
Dishonor

00:04:49.490 --> 00:04:55.490
Chapter 2

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:19.950
Hello.

00:05:21.190 --> 00:05:23.900
German potatoes
and schnitzel.

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:25.060
Thank you.

00:05:46.950 --> 00:05:52.110
I must thank you for
saving me this afternoon.

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:55.800
Since I did not have an opportunity
to thank you properly...

00:05:55.800 --> 00:06:02.010
...I would like to invite you to
dinner if you have no other plans.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:06.230
I will be at a restaurant called
Rhinegold; I'd like you to join me.

00:06:10.960 --> 00:06:13.640
I was planning
on a light supper.

00:06:16.040 --> 00:06:19.050
It's a little troublesome, but
I wouldn't want him to think...

00:06:19.050 --> 00:06:21.650
...that I declined the invitation
because of his reputation.

00:06:22.360 --> 00:06:27.000
Besides, it might be a chance to gather information for Detective Hoffmann's investigation.

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:41.970
Thank you for
coming, Commander.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.660
Thank you for the
cordial invitation.

00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.180
Don't mention it.

00:06:50.970 --> 00:06:55.150
To tell you the truth,
I thought you might not come.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:59.470
I am not exactly a
man of good reputation.

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:02.750
I see he's felt hurt
enough in his life.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.480
I'm glad that I
accepted his invitation.

00:07:26.900 --> 00:07:31.730
By the way, do you happen to know
the man who assaulted you ?

00:07:32.310 --> 00:07:34.560
I have no idea.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.390
I told that to
the police, too.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:43.480
A drug-addled man doesn't necessarily
need a cause to attack people, I think.

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:54.210
It's been ten years since I was last
here; I've come to see my old friends.

00:07:54.210 --> 00:07:57.480
They're due to
arrive tomorrow.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:02.470
We met here for the
first time, forty years ago.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:08.810
By we, I mean Mr. and
Mrs. Basel, and myself.

00:08:08.810 --> 00:08:15.200
At that time, Christopher von Basel and
I had just graduated from military school.

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.850
Weren't you two together
at military school ?

00:08:18.850 --> 00:08:22.310
Well, perhaps I'm
not explaining it well.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:26.700
Christopher and I had
become friends before that.

00:08:26.700 --> 00:08:31.210
The one I met here for the
first time is his wife, Johanna.

00:08:40.320 --> 00:08:43.680
I suppose people are
capable of aging gracefully.

00:08:45.660 --> 00:08:50.730
She's different from the court
ladies I saw at Lady Annerose's.

00:08:50.730 --> 00:08:52.300
She's a beautiful lady.

00:08:53.160 --> 00:08:54.610
Yes.

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:06.550
Yes, she was beautiful
when she was young.

00:09:06.550 --> 00:09:08.660
And she still is, even though
she's sixty years old now.

00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:15.800
Young man, there is an unbridgeable
difference between being young and being old.

00:09:15.800 --> 00:09:19.090
Being young means trying
to seek and gain something...

00:09:19.090 --> 00:09:22.810
...while being old means trying not
to lose something you already have.

00:09:22.810 --> 00:09:29.430
That, of course, doesn't tell the
whole story, but it certainly is true.

00:09:30.460 --> 00:09:31.650
And she...

00:09:32.550 --> 00:09:37.290
...I mean Johanna, ages
beautifully, as is so befitting for her.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:40.340
It's something I can never do,
no matter how much I try.

00:09:40.340 --> 00:09:45.150
My Lord, I presume you have
something that you can lose ?

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:50.780
No, I've already
lost what I can lose.

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:55.610
You can guess,
can't you ?

00:09:55.610 --> 00:10:00.800
I proposed to her
one year after we met.

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:07.590
I mustered my courage and asked
her to be my companion for life...

00:10:11.330 --> 00:10:13.700
She rejected you ?

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:17.550
No, that's not quite right.

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:23.300
She didn't reject me, she never
considered me as a man in the first place.{, as a man.}

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:30.490
When she said, "You're a nice
person," I knew I had no chance.

00:10:30.490 --> 00:10:34.400
Women don't look
for niceness in a man.

00:10:35.110 --> 00:10:38.760
"A nice person" is an
expression they use pityingly...

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:44.140
...to someone so shallow and uninteresting
that they sense no mystery in him.

00:10:44.140 --> 00:10:45.460
Is that true ?

00:10:46.270 --> 00:10:48.400
I should think so.

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:52.520
But in any case, I did not
hold a grudge against her.

00:10:52.520 --> 00:10:56.470
I understood she was
trying not to hurt me.

00:10:56.470 --> 00:11:00.690
Besides, her existence itself
was the source of my joy.

00:11:07.860 --> 00:11:10.750
You've stayed
single ever since ?

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:15.760
I don't know if this is the
right way to look at it...

00:11:15.760 --> 00:11:19.490
...but I believe that human
passion is not limitless.

00:11:19.490 --> 00:11:24.120
I feel I used it
all up for Johanna.

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:26.700
No matter how splendid
the woman I married...

00:11:26.700 --> 00:11:31.030
...that would be, for me, no more
than a fulfillment of my obligation.

00:11:31.030 --> 00:11:34.140
And that would not be good
for the woman or myself.

00:11:38.740 --> 00:11:43.750
How could a man as wise as this
commit such a fiasco at Arlesheim ?

00:12:22.000 --> 00:12:23.710
Here you are, Commander.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:27.920
Superintendent.

00:12:27.920 --> 00:12:29.780
What can I do for you ?

00:12:29.780 --> 00:12:34.300
Oh, it's nothing urgent.

00:12:34.300 --> 00:12:41.190
But since you're cooperating with us,
I thought I should give you an update.

00:12:41.190 --> 00:12:42.710
An update ?

00:12:42.710 --> 00:12:43.750
Yes.

00:12:44.800 --> 00:12:46.280
Would you like one ?

00:12:46.710 --> 00:12:47.690
No, thank you.

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:52.110
You've already had supper
with Baron Keyserling.

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:54.160
He knows everything.

00:12:54.160 --> 00:12:55.620
If you'll excuse me.

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:03.610
I've already told you that man was a
sailor in active service, haven't I ?

00:13:03.610 --> 00:13:04.700
Yes.

00:13:04.700 --> 00:13:10.300
It bugged me, so I looked into his career
and I discovered some interesting facts.

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:19.290
He was in the Keyserling Fleet three
years ago, as a Seaman 2nd class.

00:13:19.290 --> 00:13:20.090
What ?

00:13:20.090 --> 00:13:22.400
That doesn't seem
like a coincidence.

00:13:22.400 --> 00:13:25.300
Keyserling is the
assailant's former superior...

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:29.620
...though more or less an untouchable
presence, yet the guy assaulted him.

00:13:29.620 --> 00:13:31.320
Yes, but...

00:13:31.320 --> 00:13:38.300
Baron Keyserling says he has no idea
who the assailant is, and I know that.

00:13:38.300 --> 00:13:44.110
Actually, I also doubt that a fleet commander
would remember one low-ranking sailor.

00:13:44.110 --> 00:13:48.430
I wouldn't say the Baron was
lying to us just based on this.

00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:55.650
But wouldn't it be intuitive to think that there's
a thread of suspicion running through all this ?

00:13:56.610 --> 00:14:00.300
Are you saying that Baron Keyserling
is the leader of the drug organization...

00:14:00.300 --> 00:14:02.940
...to whom the aforementioned
anonymous tip alludes ?

00:14:02.940 --> 00:14:05.920
No, no, I wouldn't
quite go that far.

00:14:05.920 --> 00:14:09.660
Besides, even if - and I'm only
saying "if" - that were true...

00:14:09.660 --> 00:14:13.590
...that still wouldn't explain why he
was assaulted by the drug addict.

00:14:13.590 --> 00:14:18.800
But like I said before,
this is the only lead we have.

00:14:18.800 --> 00:14:23.920
It's like hanging onto a straw; we
have to untangle the case from here.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.060
Sieg, Sieg !

00:14:58.440 --> 00:14:59.980
Wake up, Sieg !

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.600
L...Lady Annerose...

00:15:16.700 --> 00:15:17.970
Poison gas ?

00:15:18.290 --> 00:15:20.650
No, this is...

00:15:46.250 --> 00:15:47.410
Lady Annerose...

00:15:48.130 --> 00:15:49.950
Lady Annerose saved me.

00:15:52.540 --> 00:15:53.190
Commander !

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:55.990
Commander Kircheis,
are you all right ?

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:10.050
We've found a large amount of carbon
dioxide inside the air conditioning duct.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:16.980
I think someone threw
in dry ice, vaporized it...

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:20.660
...and released it inside your room
in an attempt to suffocate you.

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:24.020
In the morning, no trace
of anything would be found.

00:16:24.020 --> 00:16:26.590
How clever.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.140
I agree.

00:16:28.140 --> 00:16:30.510
It was a close call.

00:16:30.510 --> 00:16:33.310
We were watching out
for your well-being.

00:16:34.850 --> 00:16:39.830
By the way, when you had dinner
with Baron Keyserling last night...

00:16:39.830 --> 00:16:43.200
...did you say something
that could alarm him ?

00:16:44.400 --> 00:16:47.420
So you think
he's the culprit ?

00:16:48.170 --> 00:16:50.860
I'm considering it just
as one of the possibilities.

00:16:50.860 --> 00:16:53.990
But in the initial case,
he almost became a victim.

00:16:54.370 --> 00:16:57.150
It may have been just an act.

00:16:57.150 --> 00:17:01.300
In serial murder cases, it's
fairly common in mystery stories...

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.620
...that the victim who almost
gets killed but doesn't...

00:17:03.620 --> 00:17:06.200
...sometimes turns out to be
the real culprit in the end.

00:17:06.200 --> 00:17:08.750
In other words,
you suspect him.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:12.860
It's possible this could be just
a bias or presupposition on my part.

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:20.850
But we must find clues somewhere
that will lead us to the truth.

00:17:21.800 --> 00:17:28.650
If we act, they'll react, and in
fact, someone tried to kill you.

00:17:28.650 --> 00:17:31.200
We must consider it
a challenge against us.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.460
You say "we."

00:17:35.920 --> 00:17:39.560
It seems I've been
useful to you as a decoy.

00:17:39.560 --> 00:17:43.630
When you came to talk to
me in public last night...

00:17:43.630 --> 00:17:46.310
...wasn't it meant to draw the
assailant's attention to us ?

00:17:46.890 --> 00:17:49.160
That's harsh.

00:17:49.160 --> 00:17:51.530
I don't know
how to respond.

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:54.950
But I did come to rescue you
in a pinch to make it up to you.

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:56.590
Let's call it even.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:58.500
That's fine.

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:02.900
But we can't spotlight Baron Keyserling
as a suspect quite yet for this, can we ?

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:05.310
No, Commander.

00:18:05.310 --> 00:18:10.710
I do have other reasons for
suspecting Baron Keyserling.

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:16.350
The reason the military distributes the drug to its soldiers is to make them forget their fear of dying..

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:19.980
...but there is another thing
that benefits the commanders.

00:18:19.980 --> 00:18:25.900
In other words, the drug becomes
an invisible chain on the addicts...

00:18:25.900 --> 00:18:31.000
...and if the commanding officers
are the ones distributing the drug...

00:18:31.000 --> 00:18:35.740
...the soldiers have no choice but to pledge
complete obedience to their superiors.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:37.200
That's a scary prospect.

00:18:38.650 --> 00:18:44.860
Commanding officers can give ruthless orders
without the fear of being shot in the back.

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:49.230
People can be
tempted by the drug.

00:18:49.230 --> 00:18:51.450
Certainly, it is
not inconceivable.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:52.850
But...

00:18:52.850 --> 00:18:57.650
I went to war as a soldier
for about five years.

00:18:57.650 --> 00:19:04.160
To be truthful, a sadistic commander
is worse than a faceless enemy soldier.

00:19:05.680 --> 00:19:12.650
I am fairly thick-skinned, so I served
my term and was discharged.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:18.650
But there were some who were constantly bullied by their superiors and committed suicide in the end.

00:19:18.650 --> 00:19:20.950
However, their records say
they died on the battlefield.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:24.890
The Superintendent criticizes
the military so openly.

00:19:24.890 --> 00:19:29.370
Is it because he trusts me,
or is he belittling me ?

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:37.320
When you think about it, the loyalty of
a soldier is essentially like a narcotic.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:42.550
When you're under its influence, you
feel like you're floating in a warm ocean.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:47.010
But once it wears off, you'll
find yourself in shambles.

00:19:58.860 --> 00:20:01.490
It seems you do
not agree with me.

00:20:02.020 --> 00:20:04.900
I do feel
I went too far.

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:09.150
It's an impudent request, but I'd be 
grateful if you could forget what I just said.

00:20:10.070 --> 00:20:11.160
Please don't worry.

00:20:11.160 --> 00:20:12.990
I'm a forgetful person.

00:20:14.990 --> 00:20:16.580
It's all finished.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:17.830
Good work.

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:20.520
Well, shall we go ?

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:23.300
By the way...

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:27.660
...a retired Vice Admiral named Basel and
his wife are due to arrive here today, but...

00:20:28.430 --> 00:20:34.690
Vice Admiral Basel and his wife already
arrived, the day before yesterday.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:37.580
Are you sure, Superintendent ?

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:39.490
Yes, I'm certain.

00:20:39.490 --> 00:20:45.920
We have to take good care of high-ranking
military officials like that, retired or not.

00:20:45.920 --> 00:20:47.440
Is something the matter ?

00:20:47.440 --> 00:20:48.560
No.

00:20:48.560 --> 00:20:50.030
It must be my misunderstanding.

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:53.200
Well then.

00:20:53.200 --> 00:20:54.250
We'll go now.

00:21:20.800 --> 00:21:21.650
Good morning.

00:21:22.100 --> 00:21:23.350
Good morning.

00:21:28.410 --> 00:21:32.080
Black beer, mixed and
shaken with eggs and honey.

00:21:34.010 --> 00:21:34.880
Very good, sir.{I understand.}

00:21:37.200 --> 00:21:39.130
You're not hungry ?

00:21:39.130 --> 00:21:39.960
No.

00:21:39.960 --> 00:21:41.160
I'm not well.

00:21:41.780 --> 00:21:43.900
That's not good.

00:21:43.900 --> 00:21:46.570
But since you're young,
you'll get better quickly.

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:50.130
He seems to be unaware of
the incident this morning.

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:55.550
About the Mr. and Mrs. Basel
you talked about last night...

00:21:55.550 --> 00:21:56.650
Eh ?

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:59.570
Did you say
they'll arrive today ?

00:21:59.570 --> 00:22:01.160
Yes, I did.

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:08.610
The Baron seems to think
the Basels are arriving today.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:13.290
If they stay in their hotel room
and use room service for meals...

00:22:13.290 --> 00:22:15.690
...they could go without
being seen by the Baron.

00:22:15.690 --> 00:22:19.110
But why did the Basels have
to lie to their old friend...

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:23.100
...whom they'll be seeing for
the first time in ten years ?

00:22:24.530 --> 00:22:27.570
Questions sprang up
inside Kircheis's mind.

00:22:27.570 --> 00:22:30.800
He was initially an unwitting participant
in this unexpected turn of events...

00:22:30.800 --> 00:22:33.130
...but because his life
was put in danger...

00:22:33.130 --> 00:22:36.690
...and also because there was something
else that touched a chord inside him...

00:22:36.690 --> 00:22:39.710
...he came to the point where
he could not withdraw from it.

00:22:38.850 --> 00:22:41.900
To be continued

00:22:45.400 --> 00:22:50.050
[ Time to Mourn, Time to Celebrate ]

00:22:45.400 --> 00:22:50.050
Ending Theme

00:22:45.400 --> 00:22:50.050
Vocals: Ogura Kei

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:56.530
Kircheis:

00:22:51.900 --> 00:22:56.530
Hironaka Masashi

00:22:52.370 --> 00:23:08.650
Even when I feel empty and want to throw away my life, to die...

